Thus we can add: if (self.isVisible() && (opts.field === document.activeElement || opts.field.contains(e.target))) ... but simpler: if (self.isVisible() && opts.field === document.activeElement). Because we only want to react when the field has focus.

Edge case: If the picker is bound to a trigger (like a button) and the field is hidden? Not needed.

Thus edit: In _onKeyChange function, wrap the switch inside an if that also checks that opts.field === document.activeElement.

But we must consider that the pikaday instance might be used without a field (e.g., just attached to container). In that case opts.field may be null; we should then maybe allow keyboard navigation? Probably not needed. We'll keep as is: if field exists and is activeElement.

